        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. THE SANITARY WORKS COMMITTEE is prepared to receive TENDERS for Repairs to STEAM-JACKETTED DRYER. Tenders to be sent in by Monday, Bth May, 1916. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. Further particulars may be obtained from the undersigned. R. WILSON, Manager. Longford Depot, Warrington, 25th April, 1916.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. THE SANITARY WORIiS COMMITTEE invite TENDERS for the supply of 30 TONS of good CLOVER HAY, to be delivered at Howley Central Sanitary Depot at such times and in such quantities as the Committee may direct. Tenders to be sent in securely fastened envelope, endorsed "Tender for Tray," and addressed "The Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington.', To be sent in not later than Wednesday, May 3rd, 1916. Sample to be sent with tender. The Committee reserve to themselves the right to accept or reject the whole or part of any tender. • JAMES J. A. PARFITT, Cleansing Superintendent. Cleansing Department, • April 27th, 1916.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ELECTRICITY DEPARTMENT. The ELECTRICITY ;Aid TRAMWAYS COM- MITTEE invite TENDERS for EXTENSION OF BUILDINGS. Specification and Form of Tender may be obtained at- the office of Mr. S. P., Sileock, architect, 6, Egypt-street, Warrington, where drawings may be seen on payment of one guinea, which will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide Tender. Five shillings will be charged for extra copies of Specification. Tenders, addressed to the Chairman of the Electricity and Tramways Committee, Town Hall, Warrington," must be sealed with wax and endorsed 'Tender for Extension of Build- ings," and delivered not later than 12 o'clock noon on Tuesday, 16th May, 1916. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. F. V. L. MATHIAS, Borough Electrical &amp; Tramways Engineer. Howley, Warrington.</p>
